{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 What does NOT leave your browser\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Original text} \u8212- only one-way hashes are transmitted, never the source text. A hash cannot be reversed to reconstruct the text.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Email addresses} \u8212- HB reads sender addresses in Gmail for the authorization check, but does not store or transmit them.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Browsing history} \u8212- HB has no concept of \u8220"history\u8221". It scans only the currently-visible page on demand.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b IP-derived data on the application side} \u8212- the HB backend application reads zero request IPs. Rate-limiting is performed at the network edge (Vercel Firewall) without storing IP-derived data in HB systems.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Why we can make these claims\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The built extension code ({\f1 dist/}) is published in this repository for independent audit \u8212- readable JavaScript identical to what your browser runs. The GDPR-critical cryptographic core of the backend (keyed-HMAC author marker per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "../PRIVACY.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PRIVACY.md
}}}
 \u167 ?10.2) is published as a public audit reference at {\f1 audit-references/backend/hmac.ts}. The full Backend behavior \u8212- particularly the zero-IP-on-application-side guarantee \u8212- is documented in the architecture notes available on request and can be reviewed by qualified third-party auditors under NDA. The on-chain registry is by definition public and auditable.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The full Privacy Policy is at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kicktech.io/privacy"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
www.kicktech.io/privacy
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 11. Beta program\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Current state\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Test blockchain} \u8212- registrations are made on Base Sepolia (Base\u8217's test network), not Base mainnet. This is honest beta: real cryptography, real network behavior, real on-chain transactions, but on a test chain so no real-money exposure.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Free} \u8212- registrations cost nothing during beta. As infrastructure scales and we move to mainnet, registration packages will be available (a free tier for individuals is expected to remain).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Throughput limits} \u8212- the gateway and registration endpoint are rate-limited to protect against abuse:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Per-session: ~5 registrations per 5-minute window, ~15 per hour.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Per-IP (network edge): 10 registrations per 5-minute window.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Congestion handling} \u8212- during traffic spikes, you may see \u8220"service busy, try again in a moment\u8221" responses. This is expected; retry after a few seconds.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Snapshot latency} \u8212- 5 to 50 minutes between successful registration and visible badge for all readers.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Roadmap\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Mainnet migration} \u8212- planned after Phase 0 stability is demonstrated.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Special beta-testing focus: Facebook, Messenger, and X.} These platforms are already listed as supported (see \u167 ?7), but their dynamic content patterns and DOM-structure variability mean a substantially larger volume of real-world coverage data than current beta has produced is needed before they can be considered fully battle-tested. {\b Reports from beta testers using these platforms at scale are particularly valuable.} Keyed-HMAC author anti-spoofing for X timeline, LinkedIn personal, and Facebook wall is implemented; further DOM-structure heuristics for edge cases continue to be added as data comes in.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Mobile apps} \u8212- out of scope. The technical and security reasons for the desktop-Chromium-only design are described in \u167 ?7.\sa180\par}
