}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b KT-token}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 A short authentication token of the form {\f1 KT-XXXXXX}, derived from a per-installation seed and the current 10-minute time window. Rotates automatically.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b KTOR}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 KickTech Origin Registry \u8212- the umbrella family of services for content authenticity, comprising HB, KTOR Premium, and KTOOR.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b HB}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 HumanBadge, this extension. The lightweight, popular-use tier of KTOR. No identity verification of registrants; text hashing only.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b KTOR Premium}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 The full-featured institutional tier of KTOR. Includes verified-issuer authentication, image-content and signature-block hash registration, organizational workflows, SLAs, integration support. For companies, public institutions, and government agencies. Contractual.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b KTOOR}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 KickTech Origin Open Registry. A subset of KTOR offered pro bono in narrow scope to selected large state institutions, banks, and critical-infrastructure operators by KickTech invitation, for testing protection use-cases against fraud passing through existing state-run reporting systems.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Issuer authentication}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 A process (specific to KTOR Premium and KTOOR, not present in HB) where institutional registrants prove verified identity before their registrations carry the institutional-trust signal.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Hash}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 A one-way cryptographic fingerprint. Two identical inputs produce the same hash; any change produces a completely different hash. Cannot be reversed to reconstruct the original.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b On-chain}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Recorded on a public blockchain (Base Sepolia during beta). Anyone can audit on-chain data.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b SimHash}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 A similarity-preserving hashing scheme used to fingerprint visible text in a way that is robust to minor formatting differences but sensitive to content edits.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Snapshot}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 The gateway\u8217's locally-cached view of the on-chain registry, refreshed periodically. Trades a small amount of latency for substantial performance gains.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Proof of action}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 The principle that HB attests to a specific publishing act by a specific account holder at a specific moment \u8212- not to the publisher\u8217's identity, humanity, or institutional officialness.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Keyed HMAC}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 A one-way function {\f1 HMAC-SHA256(K, value)} that produces a 256-bit fingerprint from which the original {\f1 value} cannot be recovered without the secret key {\f1 K}. HB uses a keyed HMAC of the author handle, with a fresh per-registration {\f1 K} held server-side, to bind person-publication registrations to their author without writing the handle on-chain in clear. See PRIVACY.md \u167 ?10.2.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx4320\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Cryptographic erasure}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 A way of honoring the GDPR right to erasure (Art. 17) in systems where the underlying storage is immutable (like a public blockchain). Instead of deleting the on-chain entry \u8212- which is impossible \u8212- the secret key that makes the on-chain value meaningful is deleted, rendering the on-chain value permanently irreversible. HB uses this to erase author-handle HMAC markers on request. See PRIVACY.md \u167 ?9.2a and \u167 ?10.2.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
